# fixedbugs, defect 2651, 2026-11-21: `m.Pair(a: 1, b: 2).a`, a field read on
# a record built inline and named through its module, was refused
# `dot_on_a_record_name`, *names a record*, with a guessed fix writing `::`,
# where `Pair(a: 1, b: 2).a` in the module that declares `Pair` is accepted.
#
# The cause: for a construction through a module, `m.Pair(...)`, the
# resolver records the record on the call as it records it on the record's
# name, and the checker read that as the base naming a record. It now asks
# the base expression's own form first: only a name, `Pair` or `m.Pair`,
# names a record, and a construction is a value
# (`selfhost/check/field_names.hero`).
#
# The shapes beside it, each read as it is in the declaring module: a nested
# record read through two fields; a function called on the inline value, and
# a built-in on its field; a read where the position asks for an `i64`; a
# read in a string's hole; and a variant built through the module, its case's
# field read through `match`.
use m

function twice(p: m.Pair) -> i64
    return p.a * 2

function size(s: m.Shape) -> i64
    return match s
        .circle c => c.r
        .square q => q.side

function main()
    print(m.Pair(a: 1, b: 2).a)
    print(m.Outer(inner: m.Inner(x: 5), tag: "t").inner.x)
    print(m.Pair(a: 3, b: 4).twice(), " ", m.Pair(a: 3, b: 4).b.to_str())
    n: i64 = m.Pair(a: 6, b: 7).b
    print(n + m.total(m.Pair(a: 1, b: 1)))
    print(f"{m.Pair(a: 8, b: 9).b}")
    print(size(.square(side: 10)))
